<title>USA: Exxon in Vietnamese oil venture.</title>
<headline>Exxon in Vietnamese oil venture.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp. said Thursday its Esso Eastern unit and Vietnam's Eastern Investment Co. have agreed to a joint venture that will sell petroleum products.</p>
<p>The venture, known as Esso East Vietnam Co. Ltd., will be 70 percent owned by Esso Eastern and 30 percent by Eastern Investment, a commercial enterprise of the Vietnamese government, Exxon said.</p>
<p>The joint venture company will build and operate facilities in Nhabe, Ho Chi Minh City, Exxon said.</p>
</text>
